Operating profit fell to $1.9 billion (1.28% of sales) in 2025 from $3.8 billion (2.62% of sales) in 2024. [1] The biggest single factor was $2.5 billion of fulfillment network impairment and related charges included in 2025 results. [1]

As a share of sales, the 134 basis point decline was primarily attributed to higher OG&A expenses, depreciation and amortization expenses, and the LIFO charge, partly offset by a higher FIFO gross margin rate. [1] The LIFO charge itself was $157 million in 2025 versus $95 million in 2024, reflecting higher product cost inflation. [2]

Other adjusted items also differed between years. The 2025 adjustments included labor dispute charges of 44, store closures of 100, merger-related litigation and settlement charges of 161, and a severance charge of 47 (in millions), while 2024 included merger-related costs of 684. [3] Excluding these items, adjusted FIFO operating profit rose 4.9% to $4,905 million [4], so the underlying result improved while reported operating profit dropped.